{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793972119,"nonce":"9ir64jZrfAH02B1s0Z3tU2X9D/I=","title":"An id rule with :checked or :disabled never applies; only hover, active and focus do","message":"`#cb:checked { background: #228844 }` and `#cb:disabled { ... }` have no effect on an element whose id is `cb`. The same rule written with a class (`.blinc-checkbox:checked`) applies. `#cb:hover` applies.\n\nReproduction (blinc_cn tests, the scenario harness in checkbox_states.rs, widget `checkbox(signal).id(\"cb\").label(\"Accept\")`):\n- checked, no app rule: box fill is the UA checked fill (0.490,0.659,1.000).\n- checked + `#cb:checked { background: #228844 }`: box fill stays 0.490,0.659,1.000. With `.blinc-checkbox:checked` it becomes 0.133,0.533,0.267.\n- disabled + `#cb:disabled { background: #228844 }`: fill unchanged; with `.blinc-checkbox:disabled` it applies.\n\nCause: RenderTree::apply_state_styles (renderer/stylesheet/state.rs) resolves an element's id rules for Hover, Active, Focus and FocusVisible only. Checked and Disabled are matched through element attributes (selectors.rs), which the id-rule path never consults.\n\nWhy it went unseen: the checkbox golden (crates/blinc_cn/tests/checkbox_states.golden) showed `#cb:checked` working at 02159143, then stopped reaching the checked state after d4bb38a6, because a box click reached both the box and its row and toggled twice. aa2fb930 made a click toggle once, which exposed the missing rule and failed the golden. The golden is re-blessed with the current output; re-bless it when this is fixed (the \"core under hover and checked rules\" scenario should then show #228844 once checked).\n\nScope to check: any app rule of the form `#id:checked` or `#id:disabled`. The book and Skills.md show `#btn:disabled`, so the documented form is affected.","files":null}]}